// One head tuple, two firings of one rule (BENCH-135 "2 firings"; the property of the repeated-firings test in
// Molly's provenance suite, R06 §12.6), written for this corpus: `route` joins `link` and `hop` on the relay R, which
// the head drops, so route(n, "d") is derived once through relay r1 and once through relay r2. Blossom golden corpus,
// re-derived (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

route(N, Dst) :- link(N, R, Dst), hop(N, R, Dst);

link("n", "r1", "d")@1;
link("n", "r2", "d")@1;
hop("n", "r1", "d")@1;
hop("n", "r2", "d")@1;
